info
# Issue #1476: a rework dispatch adopted a foreign checkout of the PR branch
# (a worktree the orchestrator did not create) instead of looping on
# worktree_foreign_writer forever. Info, not warning: adoption is the intended
# recovery — the checkout was verified clean, not the repo's main checkout,
# and free of any live foreign writer — but the event stays grep-able because
# a borrowed checkout has different teardown/ownership semantics (it is never
# removed) and an operator investigating a foreign worktree's mutations should
# be able to see which dispatch borrowed it.
